From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chelovechishee <261262090+chelovechishee@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 43/46] misc: add the SCSC Bluetooth service with a BlueZ front
 end

Bluetooth of the Samsung SCSC (Maxwell) WLBT subsystem: the BT service
and its shared-memory H4 transport (BSMHCP transfer rings) from the
downstream kernel of the SM-T510, without ANT, the H4 character device
and audio through the ABOX DSP; the controller address comes from
/efs/bluetooth/bt_addr ("xx:xx:xx:xx:xx:xx").

scsc_bluez.c is new: an hci_dev whose open starts the BT service, a
kthread that reads the H4 stream and reassembles it (one read can hold
several packets, a packet can be split between reads) and send that
writes H4 packets. Commands and ACL data only: the firmware has no SCO
transfer ring, SCO audio goes to the ABOX DSP.

The firmware lives on Android's VENDOR partition, and the HCI core
powers a new controller on at once; a failed first power on would keep
it from bluetoothd for good. So hci0 is registered when userspace says
the firmware can be read:
  echo 1 > /sys/module/scsc_bt/parameters/enable

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
